<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ui version="4.0">
 <class>TransformEditorHelp</class>
 <widget class="QDialog" name="TransformEditorHelp">
  <property name="geometry"><rect><x>0</x><y>0</y><width>960</width><height>760</height></rect></property>
  <property name="windowTitle"><string>Transform Editor Help</string></property>
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout">
   <item>
    <widget class="QTextBrowser" name="textBrowser">
     <property name="minimumSize"><size><width>860</width><height>600</height></size></property>
     <property name="openExternalLinks"><bool>true</bool></property>
     <property name="html">
      <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;style&gt;
h2 { margin-top: 18px; }
h3 { margin-top: 12px; }
pre { background-color: #f0f0f0; padding: 6px; }
td, th { padding: 3px 8px; }
tt { white-space: nowrap; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Transform Editor&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create new topics from the ones you loaded: drop the inputs, write the body of a function, watch the preview, press &lt;b&gt;Create&lt;/b&gt;. The result is listed in &lt;b&gt;Custom Topics&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Full guide with short videos: &lt;a href=&quot;https://plotjuggler.io/docs/toolboxes/transform-editor/&quot;&gt;plotjuggler.io/docs/toolboxes/transform-editor&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#inputs&quot;&gt;Inputs&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;#return&quot;&gt;Return values&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;#preview&quot;&gt;Preview&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;#create&quot;&gt;Create and Modify&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;#library&quot;&gt;Function Library&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;#advanced&quot;&gt;Params and Pin&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;#series&quot;&gt;Series from series&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;#api&quot;&gt;Objects: fields, methods, pj&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;#python&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;#problems&quot;&gt;When something is wrong&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;What you can make&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Series from series&lt;/b&gt;: scale, offset, derivative, the sum of two curves. The function runs once per sample, as in PlotJuggler 3.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Numbers from objects&lt;/b&gt;: the number of points of every lidar frame, the highest point, the mean brightness of an image. They become curves over the whole recording.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Objects from objects&lt;/b&gt;: a cropped point cloud, 3D markers, an overlay on a camera image. They are computed at the timeline cursor and shown in 3D and 2D views.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The editor picks the kind from the inputs: series only, or at least one object.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;inputs&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;1. Inputs&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drag topics from &lt;b&gt;Datasets&lt;/b&gt; (or from &lt;b&gt;Custom Topics&lt;/b&gt;) into &lt;b&gt;Inputs&lt;/b&gt;. Each row shows the topic, the &lt;b&gt;Var&lt;/b&gt; the function reads it by, and its type.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Var is the last part of the topic name: &lt;tt&gt;/lidar_top&lt;/tt&gt; becomes &lt;tt&gt;lidar_top&lt;/tt&gt;. Double-click a row to rename it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;inputs[&quot;/lidar_top&quot;]&lt;/tt&gt; reads the same input by its full name.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With series only, the names are &lt;tt&gt;time&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;value&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;v1&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;v2&lt;/tt&gt;... The radio button of a row picks which series is &lt;tt&gt;value&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A drag takes every row selected in Datasets &lt;b&gt;and&lt;/b&gt; in Custom Topics. Clear the other selection first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;return&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;2. Return values&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do not declare the outputs: the editor runs the function and learns them from what it returns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;You write&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;You get&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;return lidar_top:count()&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;one number, named &lt;tt&gt;value&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;return { cropped = c, max_z = top.z }&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;a point cloud &lt;tt&gt;cropped&lt;/tt&gt; and a number &lt;tt&gt;max_z&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;return { max_z = pj.unavailable(&quot;no points&quot;) }&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;no value at this instant, with a reason&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every output must be returned in every run. Returning &lt;tt&gt;nil&lt;/tt&gt; for one is an error: use &lt;tt&gt;pj.unavailable(&quot;reason&quot;)&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;preview&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;3. Preview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The function runs 300 ms after you stop typing, then at most twice a second while you move the timeline cursor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Numbers&lt;/b&gt; are drawn as a curve over the whole recording. Wheel or rectangle to zoom, Ctrl+drag or middle button to pan, right-click to undo a zoom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Objects&lt;/b&gt; are shown in a small 3D or 2D view at the cursor time. The 3D view starts in the frame of your input; an image overlay is drawn over its image input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;The status line&lt;/b&gt; says what the function returned at the cursor, or why it could not run.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;create&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;4. Create and Modify&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Create...&lt;/b&gt; asks for a name and says what will be created. The rows appear in &lt;b&gt;Custom Topics&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;tt&gt;name/output&lt;/tt&gt; for numbers; &lt;tt&gt;name&lt;/tt&gt; for a single object, &lt;tt&gt;name/output&lt;/tt&gt; when there are several.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A name cannot be empty, be an input, or contain &lt;tt&gt;__&lt;/tt&gt;. Reusing a name asks before replacing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To see an object output, open a 3D or 2D tab (&lt;b&gt;+&lt;/b&gt;, then the cube or image icon) and drag its row from Custom Topics into it. A 3D view starts in the frame of the first layer you drop. An overlay is drawn only over its own image: drag that image into the 2D view too.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To change a script later, select its row in Custom Topics and press the pencil. The button then reads &lt;b&gt;Modify&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delete is in the &lt;b&gt;...&lt;/b&gt; menu of Custom Topics. &lt;b&gt;Ctrl+Z&lt;/b&gt; undoes it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;library&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;5. Function Library&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The grid icon above the code opens the library. &lt;b&gt;Reads&lt;/b&gt; says what a function reads (series, point cloud, image...). Select one and press &lt;b&gt;Use&lt;/b&gt;: an object function is rewritten to read the Vars of your inputs. Built-in object functions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Function&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Reads&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Returns&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;points_per_frame&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;point cloud&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;its number of points&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lidar_crop&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;point cloud&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;the cloud cropped to a box, its highest z, a report, a red sphere on the highest point&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lidar_crop_map&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;point cloud&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;the same, in the &lt;tt&gt;map&lt;/tt&gt; frame when a transform exists&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;witness_of_crop&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;cropped cloud&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;a cyan sphere on its highest point&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;cam_threshold&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;image&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;an overlay on the pixels brighter than 128&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;cam_annotations&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;point cloud&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;a rectangle and a label on the front camera&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;depth_cloud&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;depth image + camera info&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;a point cloud&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;advanced&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;6. Params and Pin (Advanced &amp;gt;)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Params (JSON)&lt;/b&gt;: an object handed to the script as &lt;tt&gt;params&lt;/tt&gt;. With &lt;tt&gt;{&quot;half&quot;: 6}&lt;/tt&gt; the script reads &lt;tt&gt;params.half&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pin at current time&lt;/b&gt;: run once at the cursor time and keep that result while the cursor moves. Only object outputs are kept: one instant gives no curve, so number outputs get no row.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;series&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;7. Series from series&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;return value * 2 + 1          -- scale and offset
return (value + v1) / 2       -- average of two series
return math.log(value)        -- Luau math library&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;State between samples goes in &lt;b&gt;Global Variables&lt;/b&gt;, which runs once before the first sample. Difference between consecutive samples: Global Variables&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;prev = nil&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and the function&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;if prev == nil then
  prev = value
  return nil
end
local diff = value - prev
prev = value
return diff&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Differences with PlotJuggler 3: &lt;tt&gt;time&lt;/tt&gt; is seconds since the start of the session; &lt;tt&gt;return a, b&lt;/tt&gt; creates two series (&lt;tt&gt;name/a&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;name/b&lt;/tt&gt;) and no longer changes the timestamp; returning &lt;tt&gt;nil&lt;/tt&gt; skips the sample; tables of points are not supported. &lt;b&gt;Batch Functions&lt;/b&gt; applies one function to many series, with a prefix or suffix for the new names.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;api&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;8. Objects: fields, methods and pj&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An object input (a point cloud, an image...) gives you three kinds of things. Full list: &lt;a href=&quot;https://plotjuggler.io/docs/reference/scripting-api/&quot;&gt;plotjuggler.io/docs/reference/scripting-api&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Fields: data the object carries&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read them by name, with a dot, in Luau and in Python: &lt;tt&gt;cloud.frame_id&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;image.width&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;image.timestamp_ns&lt;/tt&gt;. They are read-only: &lt;tt&gt;cloud.frame_id = &quot;map&quot;&lt;/tt&gt; is an error. The raw bytes (points, pixels) are not a field: use the methods below. Reading a field that is a list (&lt;tt&gt;overlay.points&lt;/tt&gt;) copies the whole list into the script: on a large overlay that can exceed the script memory limit (64 MB). Use &lt;tt&gt;overlay:count()&lt;/tt&gt; to count its points.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Methods: computations on the object&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They return a new value or a new object; the input is never changed. Luau calls methods with a colon, &lt;b&gt;&quot;:&quot;&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;cloud:count()&lt;/tt&gt;); Python with a dot, &lt;b&gt;&quot;.&quot;&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;cloud.count()&lt;/tt&gt;). In Luau, &lt;tt&gt;cloud:count()&lt;/tt&gt; is short for &lt;tt&gt;cloud.count(cloud)&lt;/tt&gt;: the colon passes the object itself, so &lt;tt&gt;cloud.count()&lt;/tt&gt; fails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Object&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Methods&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;point cloud&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;count()&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;bounds()&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;crop_box{min=, max=}&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;filter(channel, op, value)&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;extreme_point(channel, &quot;max&quot;)&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;xyz_points()&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;transform(tf)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;image&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;decode()&lt;/tt&gt; gives the decoded pixels, which have &lt;tt&gt;pixel(x, y)&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;to_gray()&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;crop(x, y, w, h)&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;threshold(op, value)&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;stats()&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;depth image&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;to_point_cloud(camera_info)&lt;/tt&gt;, optional &lt;tt&gt;{step=, max_depth=}&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;video frame&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;frame_at(t_ns)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;image overlay&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;count()&lt;/tt&gt;: its number of points, without copying them&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Methods chain: &lt;tt&gt;image:decode():to_gray():threshold(&quot;&amp;gt;&quot;, 128)&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;pj: functions that belong to no object&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A library, like &lt;tt&gt;math&lt;/tt&gt;: its functions ask the session or build new objects from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Function&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;pj.unavailable(reason)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;an output with no value at this instant (not an error)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;pj.tf.lookup(target, source)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;the transform between two frames at this instant, or &lt;tt&gt;nil, reason&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;pj.tf.frames()&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;pj.tf.now&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;the frame names; the evaluation time in nanoseconds&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;pj.scene.new{...}&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;new 3D markers (&lt;tt&gt;frame_id&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;id&lt;/tt&gt;): &lt;tt&gt;:sphere{center=, diameter=, color=}&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;:cube{...}&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;:line_strip{...}&lt;/tt&gt;, then &lt;tt&gt;:finish()&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;pj.annotations.new{...}&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;a new 2D overlay on &lt;tt&gt;image_topic&lt;/tt&gt;: &lt;tt&gt;:points{...}&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;:circle{...}&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;:text{...}&lt;/tt&gt;, then &lt;tt&gt;:finish()&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;pj.typeof(x)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;the object&#x27;s type name&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Colors are &lt;tt&gt;{r, g, b, a}&lt;/tt&gt; from 0 to 255. Sizes are diameters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;python&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;9. Python&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Select &lt;b&gt;Python&lt;/b&gt;. The body is the inside of &lt;tt&gt;def evaluate(inputs, params):&lt;/tt&gt;, with the same Vars.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;cropped = lidar_top.crop_box(min=[-10, -10, -2], max=[10, 10, 3])
return {&quot;cropped&quot;: cropped, &quot;count&quot;: cropped.count()}&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Methods use a dot, &lt;b&gt;&quot;.&quot;&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;cloud.count()&lt;/tt&gt;); &lt;tt&gt;pj.tf.lookup&lt;/tt&gt; returns a pair &lt;tt&gt;(transform, reason)&lt;/tt&gt;; only &lt;tt&gt;math&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;cmath&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;statistics&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;json&lt;/tt&gt; can be imported. Desktop only. A layout that contains Python scripts runs them when it is opened: open such layouts only from sources you trust.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;problems&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;10. When something is wrong&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;You see&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Do this&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;No sample of /topic at the cursor&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The cursor is before that input&#x27;s first frame. Move the timeline cursor.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;The script returned no values&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Add a &lt;tt&gt;return&lt;/tt&gt;. The message lists the Vars you can read.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;`value` is not defined here&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;tt&gt;value&lt;/tt&gt; exists only with series inputs. Use the Var of the object.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;line N: ...&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;An error at line N of your function (&lt;tt&gt;globals line N&lt;/tt&gt;: Global Variables).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Preview: ...&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;PlotJuggler refused or could not run the preview; the text says why.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Create is disabled&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;It needs an input, a body and a run without error. Its tooltip says which is missing.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;A dot after a row in Custom Topics&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Blue: computing. Orange: an input is missing. Red: error. Grey: empty result. Hover the row for the detail.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;script memory limit (64 MB) exceeded&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The script holds too much at once, often from reading a long list such as &lt;tt&gt;overlay.points&lt;/tt&gt;. Use methods (&lt;tt&gt;count()&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;crop_box&lt;/tt&gt;...) instead.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;object bundle exceeds byte ceiling&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;The result is too large to keep. Crop, filter or sample it first.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;
</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QDialogButtonBox" name="buttonBox">
     <property name="orientation"><enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum></property>
     <property name="standardButtons"><set>QDialogButtonBox::Close</set></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
  </layout>
 </widget>
</ui>
